{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:0d85b79fde210d9c","name":"Defenses","source":{"id":"source:reference-0d85b79fde210d9c","title":"Defenses","revision":18097,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T19:35:06Z","sha256":"bddf65f0e8f8f56f9975d14c0c42ba16abdc6aa7cd5f89dc9dbe06180a222644","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18097","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Defenses&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-0d85b79fde210d9c","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Your Defenses represent your ability to avoid taking ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage"}," and overcome attacks to the body and mind. You have three Defense Scores:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Reflex Defense:"]}," How hard you are to hit in combat."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Fortitude Defense:"]}," Your ability to resist debilitating effect and resist being incapacitated."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Will Defense:"]}," Your willpower and your ability to resist effects that attack your mind."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Feats"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feats","referenceId":"reference:9194ccf56b9cace0"},", and Actions may grant additional bonuses to one or more of these Defenses. For example, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gamorreans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gamorreans"}," gain a +2 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," bonus to their Fortitude Defense, while a character with the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Improved Defenses"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Improved_Defenses","referenceId":"reference:bae4534e5fb194c7"}," feat gains a +1 bonus to all three Defenses.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Reflex Defense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Your Reflex Defense (abbreviated Reflex) represents how hard you are to hit in combat, and most attacks target a creature's Reflex Defense. If an opponent's attack roll equals or exceeds your Reflex Defense, the attack hits.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Character Combat"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Reflex Defense = 10 + Heroic Level or Armor Bonus + ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," Modifier + Size Modifier + ",{"tag":"a","children":["Class"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Class"}," Bonus"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Heroic Level:"]}," Your Heroic Level is the sum of all levels you have in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heroic Classes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heroic_Classes","referenceId":"reference:3db50eedfbef40fc"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scout"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scout","referenceId":"reference:8a1db462be753774"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"},") and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Prestige Classes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Prestige_Classes"}," (such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ace Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ace_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:3c2fd5c8fcea1d9d"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lord"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lord","referenceId":"reference:099f599e53fbfc32"},").\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["It does not include levels in the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," classes."]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Armor Bonus:"]}," Your Armor Bonus is determined by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor"}," you wear. If you are wearing ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor"},", add your Armor Bonus to your Reflex Defense instead of your Heroic Level.\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["This represents the difference between using your innate skill to avoid injury and counting on your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor"}," to absorb the damage from incoming attacks."]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," Modifier:"]}," Nimble targets are more difficult to hit than slow ones. Add your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," Modifier to your Reflex Defense. If you are Flat-Footed or unaware of an attack, you lose your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," bonus (but not a penalty) to your Reflex Defense.\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["If you are Helpless (for example, knocked ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unconscious"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unconscious"},"), calculate your Reflex Defense as if you had a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," score of 0 (-5 modifier)."]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Size Modifier:"]}," Smaller creatures are harder to hit than bigger ones. Apply the appropriate Size Modifier to your Reflex Defense (and only your Reflex Defense). Size Modifiers are as follows:"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"caption","children":["\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SIZE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MODIFIER\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["\n"],"rowspan":6},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SIZE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MODIFIER\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Colossal\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Medium\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+0\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Gargantuan\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Small\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+1\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Huge\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Tiny\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Large\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Diminutive\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+5\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"],"colspan":2},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Fine\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+10\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Vehicle Combat"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Reflex Defense = 10 + Armor Bonus or Pilot's Heroic Level + Vehicle's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," Modifier + Size Modifier"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Armor Bonus/Heroic Level:"]}," You can use the Vehicle's Armor Bonus instead of your own when calculating the Vehicle's Reflex Defense, or add your Heroic Level instead of an Armor Bonus."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," Modifier:"]}," A Vehicle's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," Modifier represents how well it can move out of harm's way. If the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," is Flat-Footed, or if the Vehicle is out of control, or attacked by an undetected opponent, the Vehicle loses its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," Bonus to its Reflex Defense.\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["If the Vehicle is at a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full Stop"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full_Stop","referenceId":"reference:74312a335c307e84"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disabled"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disabled"},", or powered down, it is treated as if it has a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," score of 0 (-5 penalty to Reflex Defense)."]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Size Modifier:"]}," Use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Size"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Size?action=edit&redlink=1"}," Modifier instead of your own when calculating the Vehicle's Reflex Defense:"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SIZE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MODIFIER\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["EXAMPLES\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Colossal (Station)\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Super Star Destroyer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Super_Star_Destroyer"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Death Star"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Death_Star","referenceId":"reference:45339c4ddfce5e9b"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Colossal (Cruiser)\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Imperial I"]},"-Class Star Destroyer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Imperial_I-Class_Star_Destroyer","referenceId":"reference:3ceed6afca222030"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["MC80 Star Cruiser"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/MC80_Star_Cruiser","referenceId":"reference:c121f32897ff5811"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Colossal (Frigate)\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Corellian Corvette"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Corellian_Corvette"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Tantive IV"]}],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Tantive_IV?action=edit&redlink=1"},"), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nebulon-B Frigate"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nebulon-B_Frigate"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Colossal\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["AT-AT"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AT-AT","referenceId":"reference:72b76e7d76526ae5"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Corellian YT-1300 Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Corellian_YT-1300_Transport","referenceId":"reference:93d1c99ee083429c"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Millennium Falcon"]}],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Millennium_Falcon","referenceId":"reference:9905dc607fa551e9"},")\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Gargantuan\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["AAT-1"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AAT-1","referenceId":"reference:9deed03865800f0c"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["X-Wing Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/X-Wing_Starfighter","referenceId":"reference:3633fb1b1140ece1"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Huge\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["AT-ST"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AT-ST","referenceId":"reference:42d3fc5263e8fdb5"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighter","referenceId":"reference:726e84ae35ac767c"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Large\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["74-Z Speeder Bike"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/74-Z_Speeder_Bike","referenceId":"reference:5f212506c0af4f6a"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["X-34 Landspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/X-34_Landspeeder","referenceId":"reference:dd868aa4e9ba8e11"},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Flat-Footed"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["In any battle that begins with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Surprise Round"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Surprise_Round"},", you start the battle Flat-Footed. You remain Flat-Footed until your first regular turn in the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative Order"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative_Order"},". You can't apply your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," bonus (if any) to your Reflex Defense while Flat-Footed.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Helpless"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A Helpless opponent- one who is bound, sleeping, unconscious, or otherwise at your mercy- is an easy target. You can sometimes approach a target that is unaware of your presence, get adjacent to it, and treat it as Helpless. If the target is in combat or some other tense situation, and therefore in a state of acute awareness and readiness, or if the target can use its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," bonus to improve its Reflex Defense, then that target can't be considered unaware. Furthermore, any reasonable precautions taken by the target- including stationing bodyguards, placing its back to the wall, or being able to make ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," checks- also precludes catching that target unaware and Helpless.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Melee Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Melee_Attack"}," against a Helpless opponent gains a +5 bonus on the attack roll (equivalent to attacking a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Prone"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Prone","referenceId":"reference:4d99dff1fb964110"}," target). A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ranged Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ranged_Attack"}," gets no special bonus. In addition, a Helpless opponent can't add its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," bonus (if any) to its Reflex Defense. In fact, its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," score is treated as if it were 0, so its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," modifier to Reflex Defense is -5.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Fortitude Defense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Your Fortitude Defense (abbreviated Fortitude) represents your ability to resist the effects of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Poison"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Poison"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disease"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disease"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Radiation"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Radiation","referenceId":"reference:669c428e617d7f09"},", as well as your ability to ignore effects that would incapacitate a normal being.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Character Combat"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Fortitude Defense = 10 + Heroic Level + ",{"tag":"a","children":["Constitution"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Constitution"}," Modifier + ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," Bonus + ",{"tag":"a","children":["Class"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Class"}," Bonus"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Heroic Level:"]}," Your Heroic Level is the sum of all levels you have in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heroic Classes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heroic_Classes","referenceId":"reference:3db50eedfbef40fc"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scout"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scout","referenceId":"reference:8a1db462be753774"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"},") and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Prestige Classes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Prestige_Classes"}," (such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ace Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ace_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:3c2fd5c8fcea1d9d"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lord"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lord","referenceId":"reference:099f599e53fbfc32"},").\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["It does not include levels in the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," classes."]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Constitution"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Constitution"}," Modifier:"]}," Tougher, healthier targets are more difficult to hurt than weaker ones, so you add your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Constitution"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Constitution"}," modifier to your Fortitude Defense.\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["A nonliving target (that is, any target without a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Constitution"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Constitution"}," score, such as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"},") instead adds its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," Modifier to its Fortitude Defense."]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," Bonus:"]}," Some kinds of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor"}," provide an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," Bonus to your Fortitude Defense."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Vehicle Combat"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Fortitude Defense = 10 + Vehicle's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," Modifier"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," Bonus:"]}," A Vehicle's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"}," modifier represents its overall toughness and durability."]}]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Will Defense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Your Will Defense (abbreviated Will) represents your willpower and your ability to resist certain ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Powers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Powers","referenceId":"reference:85acec94cd1ca5f3"}," and other effects that attack your mind.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Character Combat"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Will Defense = 10 + Heroic Level + ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"}," Modifier + ",{"tag":"a","children":["Class"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Class"}," Bonus"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Heroic Level:"]}," Your Heroic Level is the sum of all levels you have in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heroic Classes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heroic_Classes","referenceId":"reference:3db50eedfbef40fc"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scout"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scout","referenceId":"reference:8a1db462be753774"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"},") and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Prestige Classes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Prestige_Classes"}," (such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ace Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ace_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:3c2fd5c8fcea1d9d"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lord"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lord","referenceId":"reference:099f599e53fbfc32"},").\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["It does not include levels in the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," classes."]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"}," Modifier:"]}," Strong-willed characters are harder to influence than weak-willed ones. You add your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"}," modifier to your Will Defense.\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["When you are unconscious, you have an effective ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"}," score of 0 (-5 modifier)."]}]}]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
